1
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,400
Did I just die?

2
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:14,910
Elsa... What was that woman 
doing in the mansion?

3
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,870
This is... the graveyard?

4
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:22,850
So... right after the trial?

5
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:23,920
Or—

6
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:25,440
Emilia!

7
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,160
Subaru?

8
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:40,290
Yeah, that's right. It's me.

9
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:46,180
It wasn't me! It wasn't!

10
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,180
I know.

11
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:48,420
It's okay. Everything's okay.

12
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:51,480
Subaru...

13
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:01,820
I'm sorry.

14
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:03,410
I've finally calmed down.

15
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:04,880
Emilia...

16
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,670
Are you feeling all right?

17
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,790
Yes... because Subaru was 
there for me, I think.

18
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,090
We need to talk about the trial now.

19
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:18,430
Yeah... but I have a pretty 
good idea of what it's about.

20
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,090
It showed you your past, right?

21
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:23,600
Past?

22
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,230
How the hell do you know 
what happens in the trial?

23
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,080
You saw the ruins glowing, didn't you?

24
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,910
I was qualified to do it, too.

25
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:33,190
And...

26
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,080
I passed it.

27
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:40,870
Hmm... Young Su passed, eh?

28
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:43,820
Assuming he's not joking, 
that's quite an achievement.

29
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:45,600
If it's true, we can remove the barrier.

30
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:48,200
Garf, how does the barrier look now?

31
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,290
No changes.

32
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,250
So you lied. Drop dead.

33
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:53,590
You reached that conclusion too fast!

34
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:56,710
What's wrong, Garfiel?

35
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,840
Not a damn thing's wrong.

36
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,330
Subaru...

37
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:04,680
If that's true, how...

38
00:02:04,910 --> 00:02:06,600
What did you see?

39
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:10,520
I wouldn't say I "saw"... 
More like I "realized."

40
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:14,570
It seems like there's not just 
one of these sadistic trials.

41
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,400
There are three in total, apparently.

42
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:20,080
So... two more?

43
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:26,560
Emilia, I have a suggestion.

44
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,100
You might not like it, though.

45
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:31,810
A suggestion?

46
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:36,090
I could do the remaining trials in your place,

47
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:38,260
and pass them. That's my suggestion.

48
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,500
I want to be your strength.

49
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,760
I don't know what you saw in your past,

50
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:48,450
but if it made you cry so hard and 
look like you were in such pain...

51
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,440
I want to lend you a hand.

52
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,020
Hang on!

53
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:55,190
You've just been sayin' whatever the 
hell you want while we sit and listen,

54
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,080
but I don't want anyone but the princess,

55
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:01,780
Emilia-sama, bein' the one 
to go through the trial.

56
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:07,700
At the very least, you're the last person 
I wanna see gettin' rid of the barrier!

57
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,250
You can go through the trial 
in Emilia-sama's place.

58
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:14,000
Wait, wait, wait!

59
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,530
What? You're surprised that I'm against it?

60
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,170
You're a real dumbass, ya know that?

61
00:03:19,170 --> 00:03:20,430
No, I mean, why—

62
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,340
Subaru...

63
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:26,060
A-Are you saying you can't 
trust me with this?

64
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:26,760
Huh?

65
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:30,040
Because you saw me failing.

66
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:32,290
So you want to do it instead?

67
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:34,680
That's not it! But you shouldn't 
have to face your past if—

68
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:38,210
But if I don't face it, 
I'll never get past the trial!

69
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:40,160
If I turn my eyes away
from things I don't like,

70
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:42,200
leave them all to you, and run away...

71
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:45,660
What would be left for me then?

72
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,920
Let's stop talking about this.

73
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,040
Got a minute?

74
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:58,690
Why were you so opposed to what I suggested?

75
00:03:58,690 --> 00:03:59,500
Because—

76
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,070
Because it is what Young Ros wants.

77
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:08,470
Young Ros believes that Emilia-sama should 
be the one to liberate the Sanctuary.

78
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:11,980
And you guys back him on that?

79
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:13,440
Don't get me wrong!

80
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:16,330
I hate that son of a bitch as much as you do.

81
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:18,980
But... you get it, don't you?!

82
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:21,040
I guess...

83
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:24,830
even if the barrier disappeared and Sanctuary
 officially became part of his domain...

84
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:27,720
This land is overseen by Young Ros.

85
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,700
No one among us wishes to defy 
him and endanger our position.

86
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,240
I hope you and the others 
know that I am sorry.

87
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:37,880
It just keeps getting harder and 
harder for me to trust Roswaal.

88
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:41,400
Anyway! It's gotta be the princess 
who goes through the trial!

89
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,340
Even if you <i>are</i> qualified, 
I ain't lettin' you do it!

90
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:51,550
Damn it... Emilia...

91
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,540
<i>No, take it easy.</i>

92
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:56,770
<i>I need to figure out what 
to do about the mansion.</i>

93
00:04:57,870 --> 00:05:02,780
<i>There's no way that insane woman won't 
do anything to Rem and the new maids.</i>

94
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,570
<i>It's Frederica I'm worried about.</i>

95
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:08,240
<i>Does she have ties to Elsa somehow?</i>

96
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:13,450
<i>In any case, I need to get back 
to the mansion as fast as I can.</i>

97
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:19,170
And what is it you would like me to do?

98
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:21,760
Get the people of Arlam Village back home.

99
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:25,730
I want you to bring up that suggestion 
to Ryuzu-san and the rest.

100
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:31,110
It doesn't look like I'll be able to 
get them to agree with me this time.

101
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:32,800
"This time"?

102
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,850
Hmm... And why is that?

103
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:39,860
That Garfiel punk seems to hate my guts.

104
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:43,130
I don't have time to convince 
someone as volatile as him.

105
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:45,570
And there's one other thing.

106
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:48,200
I want to go and tell the 
people who're still in Arlam

107
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,030
that their families are safe.

108
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,790
I'm going back there alone to tell them that.

109
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:57,500
Of course, I'm also going to the mansion, 
where Frederica's planning something.

110
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,780
Ram has informed me of this.

111
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:03,040
But given what I know about her, 
Frederica would not be hasty in—

112
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,460
And what do you know?

113
00:06:04,810 --> 00:06:07,480
Frederica gave Emilia the glowing stone.

114
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,680
That's proof she's planning something!

115
00:06:12,930 --> 00:06:16,310
And if she does prove to be 
an enemy, what will you do?

116
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:20,130
I'm sorry to say so, but you 
stand no chance against her.

117
00:06:21,150 --> 00:06:24,990
Emilia's dealing with 
the barrier, you're injured,

118
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:26,820
and Otto won't have any part in all this.

119
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,080
We're stuck.

120
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:31,050
That is true, with the exception of one person.

121
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,490
If I may be blunt, I don't like this.

122
00:06:34,490 --> 00:06:37,610
You're still talking like that, Nee-sama?

123
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:40,360
With Roswaal-sama in his current condition,

124
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:42,670
I don't like the idea of leaving his side.

125
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:46,370
Yeah, but it's not like you can 
do anything for him, right?

126
00:06:46,370 --> 00:06:49,680
I couldn't believe it when I heard that 
Garfiel put those bandages on him.

127
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,340
Don't be a fool.

128
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:54,430
What if I had put them on him and 
only made his injuries worse?

129
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,120
Show a little guilt, would you?!

130
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:59,770
Makin' your triumphant return 
with a pretty girl on each arm?

131
00:06:59,770 --> 00:07:01,850
You've really got some nerve, you know that?

132
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:05,840
I didn't expect you to come out so 
early in the morning to see me off.

133
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:06,730
So you heard?

134
00:07:07,050 --> 00:07:11,670
Frankly, it pisses me off that 
this was all decided without me,

135
00:07:11,670 --> 00:07:13,030
but I ain't gonna fight it.

136
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:16,160
Really? That's good to know.

137
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,840
If you'd tried to stop me,

138
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:20,780
I would've had to throw Ram off 
into the distance as a decoy.

139
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:22,700
Like that would even work!

140
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:23,950
Would it?

141
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:24,960
How would I know?!

142
00:07:25,210 --> 00:07:26,920
You should say something to...

143
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:30,630
Ram? What's wrong?

144
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:33,540
This stupid conversation gave 
me a headache, that's all.

145
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,890
Well, I'm outta here.

146
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:40,630
I should be back tomorrow, 
so look after things until then.

147
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,400
You're not gonna say goodbye to the princess?

148
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:47,120
I'm surprised you're actually 
worried about Emilia.

149
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:50,140
But it's fine. I left her a letter.

150
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,740
By the way, don't you have 
anything to give me?

151
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:57,990
Huh? The hell are you talkin' about?

152
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:02,370
Then are you going to show 
some concern for me?

153
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:05,440
The woman you love is leaving 
to fulfill her duty.

154
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,500
Have you no desire to offer 
her some assistance?

155
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:12,220
You're only nice when you'll get 
somethin' out of it, aren't ya?

156
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:13,850
There!

157
00:08:15,450 --> 00:08:16,870
Take care of Emilia.

158
00:08:16,870 --> 00:08:20,700
Do the best you can to let her know I'm 
sorry from the bottom of my heart!

159
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,100
Tell her that yourself, damn it!

160
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,020
So, Barusu...

161
00:08:28,390 --> 00:08:30,730
Will this thing Garf gave us be of some use?

162
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,180
I don't know.

163
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:35,280
What do you think? You've known
 him longer than I have.

164
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,990
Actually, I have no idea.

165
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:39,470
Since it's part of a matching pair,

166
00:08:39,470 --> 00:08:41,140
I'm sure it means something to him.

167
00:08:44,810 --> 00:08:47,460
You've looked pretty unhappy today.

168
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,050
What you said earlier...

169
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:54,010
When you said you would throw me as a decoy.

170
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:57,500
For some reason, that bothered 
me more than I expected.

171
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:58,780
Almost as if...

172
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:02,590
something like that has really happened before.

173
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,160
Barusu?

174
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:15,980
Ram, there's something important 
I need to tell you.

175
00:09:16,870 --> 00:09:19,820
The most important thing in the world to you.

176
00:09:21,070 --> 00:09:24,250
The only thing that important 
to me is Roswaal-sama.

177
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:25,780
No, there's something else.

178
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,750
So I'm going to tell you about it.

179
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,480
There's a girl named Rem...

180
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:44,040
<i>Please don't let anything be happening.</i>

181
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,560
<i>I'm here two days earlier than last time.</i>

182
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,400
<i>If it still goes wrong,</i>

183
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,630
<i>I'll have to take off on Patrasche 
the moment I wake up in the graveyard.</i>

184
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,780
<i>If Frederica turns out to be an enemy,</i>

185
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:58,530
<i>it's crucial to know when 
she's going to take action.</i>

186
00:09:58,530 --> 00:09:58,960
Barusu?

187
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,600
<i>Should I attack or run?</i>

188
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:04,570
<i>If it's Elsa I'm dealing with, 
it'd be wise to turn tail and run.</i>

189
00:10:04,570 --> 00:10:05,640
<i>Which means...</i>

190
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,620
Barusu!

191
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:10,290
What? I was thinking about—

192
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:14,600
Welcome back, Subaru-sama.

193
00:10:15,130 --> 00:10:18,010
You returned much sooner than I expected.

194
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,160
Is something wrong, Subaru-sama?

195
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:27,520
Oh, God! You're just so cute!

196
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,680
What, what?! What is this?! Subaru!

197
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:33,540
Damn! You have no idea what I've been through!

198
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,310
Seriously... Damn it...

199
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,120
Is that...

200
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,500
Oh... It's to match the one I gave you.

201
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,920
Are you hurt?

202
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,000
No.

203
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:59,010
I'm just incredibly relieved, 
from the bottom of my heart.

204
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,470
It's good to be back, Petra.

205
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,100
If I may be blunt, I don't like this.

206
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:07,140
I feel like I've heard that before...

207
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,620
Yes, because it was sarcasm.

208
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:12,750
The cute sarcasm of a Ram who has 
been forgotten and left at a loss.

209
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:16,220
Um, you're Ram-neesama, right?

210
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:20,990
I was just hired as a new maid in 
service to the lord of the mansion.

211
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:22,030
I'm Petra.

212
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:24,120
It's a pleasure to meet you.

213
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:28,210
You seem to know your place, unlike Barusu.

214
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:30,080
Very good. I give you a passing grade.

215
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,620
By the way, Barusu, you fail.

216
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:34,730
I won't allow you to cross 
this mansion's threshold.

217
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:37,090
What was the point of coming back, then?!

218
00:11:38,810 --> 00:11:43,130
Hey, Petra... has anything weird 
happened while we were away?

219
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:44,510
Like, with Frederica?

220
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:46,200
Frederica-neesama?

221
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,470
There's nothing weird about her at all.

222
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:50,200
Is she inside right now?

223
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,490
She's out patrolling the forest barrier.

224
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:54,700
It may be a while before she gets back.

225
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:56,800
I'm not sure if our timing is good or bad.

226
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,480
What should we do, Barusu?

227
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:01,720
I want to see what she's going to do.

228
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,110
We'll wait with Rem in the meantime.

229
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,380
I'm going to get back to cleaning.

230
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:16,260
If you need anything, please call for me.

231
00:12:20,350 --> 00:12:21,890
You're nervous, huh?

232
00:12:21,890 --> 00:12:23,150
I am not.

233
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:25,100
Well, you should be.

234
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,100
It's the right reaction. I want you to be.

235
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,140
I'm so glad you're all right.

236
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:43,770
Barusu...

237
00:12:44,530 --> 00:12:45,250
What?

238
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,780
Could you leave us alone for a bit?

239
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,340
It's a start...

240
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:03,680
It's a start.

241
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:06,680
You returned sooner than 
I expected, Subaru-sama.

242
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,640
What a surprise.

243
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,980
Since Emilia-sama is not with you,

244
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:19,330
I assume the trial is not yet complete?

245
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,740
Yeah.

246
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,070
There are some things I want to ask you.

247
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:25,650
First, about this.

248
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:30,870
That is...

249
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:38,240
Garf's stone.

250
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:40,400
Yeah. So you really do know him...

251
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,760
I mean, you really are related?

252
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,510
Garf did not tell you so himself?

253
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:47,500
It's easy enough to guess from your faces.

254
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:50,350
And I imagine you're the older sibling.

255
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,860
You are correct.

256
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,180
I am Garf's...

257
00:13:57,190 --> 00:14:00,690
Garfiel's older sister by blood.

258
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,030
Answer me something.

259
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,480
Why did you use the glowing stone

260
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,910
to set a teleport trap?

261
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,020
Can't tell me that because 
of your oath, either?

262
00:14:14,570 --> 00:14:16,040
Well, this is one thing you need to—

263
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,260
Subaru-sama...

264
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,960
What do you mean by "teleport"?

265
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,600
I-I do not know how to respond to that look.

266
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,420
Wait! Wait, wait!

267
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:27,580
You won't fool me!

268
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:31,510
I know you're working with the conservatives 
who don't want the Sanctuary to be freed!

269
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:34,220
Conservatives? I do not know what you mean.

270
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:37,180
You will need to explain everything 
from the beginning...

271
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:40,860
Y-You're really not acting or signaling?

272
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:43,320
Having one-on-one time with 
Frederica in my absence?

273
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,220
It would seem you have no 
need for your life, Barusu.

274
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,490
Uh, no, I was...

275
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:56,450
Your skill at making tea hasn't 
improved since we left, I see.

276
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:00,380
Oh... but making tea is 
the one thing I excel at.

277
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:01,830
What an unlovable girl you are.

278
00:15:02,150 --> 00:15:04,100
I'm perfectly lovable.

279
00:15:04,490 --> 00:15:06,560
If I were more lovable, 
the world would be in danger.

280
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:09,320
You always have a sharp retort ready.

281
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,050
Honestly...

282
00:15:10,630 --> 00:15:12,290
How very like you.

283
00:15:12,290 --> 00:15:13,140
And?

284
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:17,690
If you don't know about the teleporting, 
why did you give Barusu the glowing stone?

285
00:15:17,690 --> 00:15:18,870
Well...

286
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:21,480
You can't tell us because of your oath?

287
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:24,190
If so, that's a pathetic excuse, Frederica.

288
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:27,400
You are right.

289
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,030
I cannot tell you anything.

290
00:15:30,390 --> 00:15:32,080
Sticking to your pathetic excuse, I see.

291
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,180
Then there's nothing more to discuss.

292
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:35,460
Hey, take it easy!

293
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:38,500
Your refusal to answer the question 
makes your betrayal clear.

294
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:41,460
We will restrain you and 
take you to the Sanctuary.

295
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:45,960
Then we can figure out who's 
been giving you your orders.

296
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,360
Yeah, but...

297
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:51,000
If you insist on taking me to the 
Sanctuary, I will not resist.

298
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,050
There, see? Even Frederica's—

299
00:15:53,570 --> 00:15:54,430
Wait, what?

300
00:15:54,430 --> 00:15:57,390
I said that I will not resist.

301
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,140
You... won't?

302
00:15:59,690 --> 00:16:00,430
Why?!

303
00:16:00,430 --> 00:16:02,200
You're awfully slow on the uptake.

304
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:05,640
Frederica can't break her 
oath of her own free will,

305
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:08,360
so you'll have to use force 
to make her, Barusu.

306
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:11,390
That's the kind of excuse she needs.

307
00:16:14,410 --> 00:16:16,720
You guys are in perfect sync.

308
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,010
Naturally.

309
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:19,910
We've known each other for nearly ten years.

310
00:16:20,970 --> 00:16:23,840
If that's all it's gonna take,
 frankly, I'm relieved.

311
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,920
I want to get out of here as soon as—

312
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:25,920
Oh, dear.

313
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:29,700
I wish you wouldn't say such unfriendly things.

314
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,480
Now, let's keep that promise we made.

315
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,160
Nee-sama...

316
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,200
Subaru...

317
00:16:47,450 --> 00:16:48,940
Run!

318
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:50,190
El Fula!

319
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,320
Partial beast transformation...
You have demihuman blood. How lovely.

320
00:16:56,510 --> 00:16:57,300
Petra!

321
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,660
I'll shred you!

322
00:17:03,330 --> 00:17:04,000
Her arm...

323
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,420
Goodness, that hurt.

324
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,210
I thought I was a goner.

325
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:12,540
I like it.

326
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:15,720
Maids in large, medium, and small, and one boy.

327
00:17:16,450 --> 00:17:19,880
I'll put you all on a table and 
compare what's inside your bellies.

328
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,060
Even Garf's pick-up lines are better!

329
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:22,710
Barusu!

330
00:17:22,710 --> 00:17:23,680
I know!

331
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,600
Shamac!

332
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:32,780
We're leaving!

333
00:17:33,350 --> 00:17:34,150
Subaru!

334
00:17:34,150 --> 00:17:35,530
Frederica!

335
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:38,640
Ul Fula!

336
00:17:45,490 --> 00:17:46,910
Frederica-neesama!

337
00:17:47,850 --> 00:17:49,830
I underestimated our opponent.

338
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:51,320
Ow...

339
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:54,160
Damn it... Did we get her?

340
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:57,300
It didn't feel like it. Who was she?

341
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,330
Rem... Beatrice...

342
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:04,050
We have to save them.

343
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:05,960
We leave them here.

344
00:18:07,110 --> 00:18:09,650
The four of us will escape 
and leave them here.

345
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:12,010
That's the best option right now.

346
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,720
What... did you...

347
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:17,490
What the hell are you saying?!

348
00:18:17,490 --> 00:18:19,650
What good will yelling do? Calm yourself.

349
00:18:19,650 --> 00:18:22,400
That's Rem inside the mansion! Your sister!

350
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:26,400
You love her, and she loves you!
You have to protect your little sister!

351
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,240
I only made the appropriate judgment.

352
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:33,440
Losing you along with Frederica and me 
would be a far greater loss for our side.

353
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:35,030
Sacrifices must be made.

354
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,650
You're talking about sacrificing—

355
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:39,050
Yes, she may be my younger sister.

356
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:43,510
I sensed that the same blood 
flows in her as in me.

357
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:47,980
But her existence itself is a blank.

358
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:51,510
Still, if she is my sister, 
this is what she would say:

359
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:57,250
"Please sacrifice me to save Roswaal-sama."

360
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:03,680
I... didn't bring you here 
to make you say that.

361
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:07,370
I believe we should save the two of them.

362
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:13,250
Both Beatrice-sama and Rem 
are also vital to our side.

363
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:17,380
M-Me, too! I think we should save them, too!

364
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,810
I agree with her!

365
00:19:18,810 --> 00:19:20,860
We're not taking a majority vote.

366
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,180
Be quiet, child.

367
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:24,790
I-I may be a child, but I'm plenty grown-up!

368
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:28,120
Frederica-neesama even said 
I'm more useful than you!

369
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,100
Frederica, what did you say to her?

370
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:35,180
Since it was my idea, I will assume 
the task of stopping the enemy.

371
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:42,360
So you're deliberately choosing 
to draw the short straw again.

372
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,800
You're just like Garf.

373
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:47,050
You girls are my precious junior colleagues.

374
00:19:47,050 --> 00:19:49,830
Also, it is incorrect to 
say I am "just like Garf."

375
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:52,710
Garf is the one who imitates me.

376
00:20:05,150 --> 00:20:07,010
So this is a beast transformation?

377
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:16,610
Petra, I am sorry for frightening you.

378
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,920
You can still talk like that?

379
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:21,070
I am still me, after all.

380
00:20:21,450 --> 00:20:24,300
You did wonderfully, 
resisting the urge to scream.

381
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,030
Yes...

382
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:28,480
Yes! Please be careful!

383
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,950
Good girl.

384
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:32,240
Ram, I leave the rest in your hands.

385
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,460
No need to remind me.

386
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,920
But if you fall too far behind, 
I'll make you regret it.

387
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:45,050
Snap out of it!

388
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:47,700
Let's go.

389
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:50,300
Right... We'll start with Rem.

390
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,150
This is bad...

391
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:02,400
This is bad. This is bad...

392
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:05,230
We've gotta hurry upstairs!

393
00:21:18,330 --> 00:21:19,710
A mabeast?!

394
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,510
This way!

395
00:21:25,970 --> 00:21:27,280
El Fula!

396
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:29,500
Why is a mabeast here?!

397
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:30,640
There's no time for questions.

398
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,870
It's here, and that's that!

399
00:21:31,870 --> 00:21:33,470
I'll go fetch the ground dragon from the stable.

400
00:21:33,470 --> 00:21:34,820
You mean Patrasche?

401
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:38,010
With a mabeast here, we'll need transportation.

402
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:41,110
Retrieve the two of them while I draw it away.

403
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,380
Fula!

404
00:21:45,530 --> 00:21:46,490
Follow me!

405
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:00,320
Okay... Now's my—

406
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,060
Subaru?!

407
00:22:04,170 --> 00:22:05,230
You're bleeding!

408
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:11,240
This is gonna hurt! Be strong!

409
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:12,720
Three, two...

410
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:24,170
Thanks...

411
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,130
But what happened to "one"?

412
00:22:27,130 --> 00:22:29,300
You were less tense this way.

413
00:22:31,770 --> 00:22:33,920
Petra... I'm sorry.

414
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:36,720
I'm always putting you in danger.

415
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:40,120
Don't say silly things like 
that! I'm grateful to you!

416
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:43,630
You always come to save me when I'm in danger!

417
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,930
So this time, it's my turn.

418
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:49,290
We'll get Rem-neesama and 
Beatrice-chan out of here,

419
00:22:49,290 --> 00:22:52,470
and escape with Ram-neesama and 
Frederica-neesama. All of us!

420
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:56,420
You're amazing, Petra. I feel so pathetic.

421
00:22:56,420 --> 00:22:57,220
You're not—

422
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:59,230
No, I didn't mean that as a complaint.

423
00:22:59,690 --> 00:23:02,520
I meant I've gotta try harder 
to be as amazing as you.

424
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,130
Let's go.

425
00:23:06,130 --> 00:23:08,780
Like you said, we're all gonna get out of here.

426
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,490
Yeah!

427
00:23:19,010 --> 00:23:19,730
Oh!

428
00:23:19,730 --> 00:23:21,120
Wh-What?!

429
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:24,300
I meant "Yes," not "Yeah"!

430
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:26,380
That is... The appropriate 
response was "Yes"!

431
00:23:26,910 --> 00:23:29,590
I'll have Frederica or Ram scold you lat—

432
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,720
...rusu! Barusu!

433
00:23:37,430 --> 00:23:40,310
That was a mistake. I should 
have come to check sooner.

434
00:23:40,310 --> 00:23:42,810
I must do what I must do.

435
00:23:42,810 --> 00:23:44,230
I'm going to do so, too.

436
00:23:44,890 --> 00:23:46,520
That's it. Very good.

437
00:23:51,150 --> 00:23:53,240
Pa...asche...

438
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:16,390
This... is...

439
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:23,350
Are you okay, Pet—

440
00:24:53,670 --> 00:24:57,100
Ah, you've finally found me!

441
00:24:57,950 --> 00:25:00,050
Where's... Frederica?

442
00:25:00,050 --> 00:25:02,260
You mean the big maid?

443
00:25:02,260 --> 00:25:03,740
Don't worry.

444
00:25:03,740 --> 00:25:05,440
She proved to be quite enjoyable.

445
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:09,150
Who sent you after us?

446
00:25:09,550 --> 00:25:12,120
I don't speak of my clients.

447
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:14,910
I do have that much courtesy, at least.

448
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:17,810
Though, since you came back 
sooner than expected,

449
00:25:17,810 --> 00:25:21,370
this didn't play out exactly 
as my directions specified.

450
00:25:21,370 --> 00:25:23,620
Not as... specified...

451
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:26,910
Two maids and one shut-in...

452
00:25:26,910 --> 00:25:29,250
It was supposed to be timed to your return.

453
00:25:31,790 --> 00:25:33,710
This is... enough.

454
00:25:33,990 --> 00:25:38,240
True. I don't want Maylie taking 
any more credit from me.

455
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:40,210
So let's end this now.

456
00:25:40,960 --> 00:25:43,180
I'll send you to meet the angels.

457
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:47,270
<i>Even if this world won't last,</i>

458
00:25:47,270 --> 00:25:49,110
<i>I won't let her hurt Rem!</i>

459
00:25:50,780 --> 00:25:51,560
<i>Rem!</i>

460
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:00,120
Why...

461
00:26:02,750 --> 00:26:04,950
Why did you save me?!

462
00:26:04,950 --> 00:26:09,920
The Maiden's Gospel

463
00:26:05,870 --> 00:26:08,120
Beatrice!

464
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:18,120


